    "created_at": "2025-09-30T09:35:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-30T09:35:06Z",
    "body": "I think that is very unlikely to happen. There is generally significant cost and risk (web compat and security) with changing the parser, so the benefit needs to be substantial.\n\nFurther, even if this nesting is allowed, the CSS table model would still be broken. Maybe `display: contents` works, but `summary` is an interactive element and using `display: contents` on interactive elements is not without issues (exposure to AT, focusability).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
